{
  "$comment": "The published core contract an extension is checked against. layers: the final layout (placement-final-v2) as it falls on the vendored closure: the kernel (core), kernel types, the standard modules that own a vendored file (trusted-match and the compliance-testing leaf own none), each of buying's eight layers as its own layer (buying/<layer>, with depends_on naming the layers directly below it; pricing and catalogs are siblings, and so are offer and execution; buying/delivery owns no vendored file), the generated assembly, the 3.x compatibility assembly (_compat: the legacy get_products product and its signal targeting option listing, removed in 4.0), and x-<name> for a file the layout places in an extension (three bridge extensions and spot-lifecycle; module schemas $ref them only under x-adcp-bridge-point annotations). Each layer has its own version, the hooks it declares (contract majors; a major changes only if the hook's schema or must-understand policy changes), and a frozen digest over the files it owns (core/placement.json). Re-stamped when the layers moved from the ten-module cut to the final layout: hook names and majors are unchanged; pricing_option and pricing_model moved to buying/pricing, commercial_terms to buying/commitment, and media_buy_state to buying/execution; the kernel gained core/webhook-activity-record.json, and kernel types gained the catalog format and core/property.json. Re-stamped again when core/patches.json applied the layout's 3.4 fixes (kernel types with registry composition, bridge points); the bundle digest moved, no payload changed. types: per-schema majors for core types an extension may $ref (default_major unless overridden). bundle_digest: JCS sha256 of the whole bundle (what an app lock pins). The build fails if any layer stops matching its digest. Re-stamped when the kernel's capabilities fragment gained the optional modules map (in _assembly): only _assembly and the bundle digest moved.",
  "adcp_version": "3.3.0",
